WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:03.412
Your app is on a phone, and something is wrong.

2
00:00:03.412 --> 00:00:04.776
A button does nothing.

3
00:00:04.776 --> 00:00:06.015
You did not find it.

4
00:00:06.015 --> 00:00:07.750
Lumi did, while you watched.

5
00:00:09.500 --> 00:00:14.068
By the end, Lumi has tested your app, and you have replayed one problem.

6
00:00:14.068 --> 00:00:17.050
You need no AI account, and you write no code.

7
00:00:18.650 --> 00:00:21.270
Open a terminal in your app folder.

8
00:00:21.270 --> 00:00:24.114
Type npx shipvo lumi, and press Enter.

9
00:00:24.114 --> 00:00:26.884
Shipvo builds a web copy of your app.

10
00:00:26.884 --> 00:00:28.605
For an iPhone, add ios.

11
00:00:28.605 --> 00:00:31.150
Android and iOS work the same way.

12
00:00:32.750 --> 00:00:34.100
Your browser opens.

13
00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.876
The phone is on the left.

14
00:00:35.876 --> 00:00:38.078
Lumi's sidebar is on the right.

15
00:00:38.078 --> 00:00:39.783
Findings starts at zero.

16
00:00:39.783 --> 00:00:41.275
Now, give Lumi a job.

17
00:00:43.750 --> 00:00:46.038
Type, test my app, and press Enter.

18
00:00:46.038 --> 00:00:49.306
Lumi taps through your app, from the start screen.

19
00:00:49.306 --> 00:00:52.574
A caption names each step, like, Tapping Checkout.

20
00:00:52.574 --> 00:00:54.600
The sidebar lists every action.

21
00:00:56.750 --> 00:00:58.177
Now look at Findings.

22
00:00:58.177 --> 00:01:00.623
Each one is something Lumi reported.

23
00:01:00.623 --> 00:01:02.458
A button that does nothing.

24
00:01:02.458 --> 00:01:04.225
A screen that stays blank.

25
00:01:04.225 --> 00:01:05.992
A network call that fails.

26
00:01:05.992 --> 00:01:07.895
Each problem is listed once.

27
00:01:07.895 --> 00:01:11.700
Coverage shows how many screens and controls Lumi tried.

28
00:01:13.300 --> 00:01:15.173
Here is the part that matters.

29
00:01:15.173 --> 00:01:17.108
Press Replay next to a finding.

30
00:01:17.108 --> 00:01:19.792
The phone repeats the steps that led to it.

31
00:01:19.792 --> 00:01:23.225
You watch the problem happen again, with your own eyes.

32
00:01:24.825 --> 00:01:26.160
Want a harder test?

33
00:01:26.160 --> 00:01:28.548
Type, try checkout with bad input.

34
00:01:28.548 --> 00:01:31.640
Lumi runs the same path with invalid values.

35
00:01:31.640 --> 00:01:35.925
A finding here means your app accepted what it should refuse.

36
00:01:37.525 --> 00:01:38.111
Fixed it?

37
00:01:38.111 --> 00:01:38.698
Prove it.

38
00:01:38.698 --> 00:01:40.326
Stop Lumi with Ctrl+C.

39
00:01:40.326 --> 00:01:42.737
Start it again with --seed 1.

40
00:01:42.737 --> 00:01:47.428
The same seed gives the same walk, so you can check that the fix worked.

41
00:01:47.428 --> 00:01:52.900
And Save as test turns a finding into a test file that fails while the bug is there.

42
00:01:54.500 --> 00:01:55.274
That is it.

43
00:01:55.274 --> 00:01:57.808
Lumi tests your app while you watch.

44
00:01:57.808 --> 00:02:00.553
Try npx shipvo lumi in your app folder.

45
00:02:00.553 --> 00:02:03.650
The guide is at shipvo.dev/learn.
